{"shortDescription":"Strong performance builds on momentum from 2025LONDON, UK / ACCESS Newswire / September 2, 2026 / Ecora Royalties PLC LSE:ECORTSX:ECOR(OTCQX:ECRAF) announces half year results for the six months ended 30 June 2026 which are available on the Group's website at www.ecoraroyalties.com and on SEDAR at…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"i","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Strong performance builds on momentum from 2025"]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["LONDON, UK / ACCESS Newswire / September 2, 2026 /"]}," Ecora Royalties PLC ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"LSE:ECOR","text":"LSE:ECOR"}},{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TSX:ECOR","text":"TSX:ECOR"}},"(OTCQX:ECRAF) announces half year results for the six months ended 30 June 2026 which are available on the Group's website at www.ecoraroyalties.com and on SEDAR at www.sedar.com. All currencies referred to within are in US dollars unless otherwise specified."]},{"type":"p","children":["Ecora is a leading critical minerals focused royalty and streaming company. Copper is at the core of the portfolio which also includes other commodities linked to the trend of electrification, energy transition, infrastructure renewal and urbanisation, digital infrastructure, robotics and energy security."]},{"type":"p","children":["Marc Bishop Lafleche, Chief Executive Officer of Ecora, commented:"]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Ecora's strong first-half performance builds on the momentum established in 2025. The core critical minerals portfolio delivered another record performance, further demonstrating its underlying cash generation potential, with revenue growth converting to a significant increase in adjusted earnings growth, highlighting the scalability of the royalty model. Strong cash generation is expected to continue to drive deleveraging in the second half of 2026, with the additional benefit of commodity price tailwinds should the price of copper, and other key commodity exposures, remain at or above current levels."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Looking forward, a number of our operating partners are targeting near-term milestones which are expected to advance the next wave of organic growth in our portfolio. Within the base metals portfolio, the evaluation of brownfield expansion opportunities are being progressed at Voisey's Bay and Mantos Blancos, alongside the greenfield Santo Domingo project that is moving towards Final Investment Decision. Elsewhere, a Definitive Feasibility Study on the Phalaborwa rare earths project continues to progress towards completion."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"This combination of strong cash generation, commodity price tailwinds, deleveraging, potential key derisking milestones underpinned by a positive fundamental outlook for copper and other critical minerals, gives us great confidence in the near and long-term outlook for Ecora.\""]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Financial highlights:"]}]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Total portfolio contribution increased 75% to $31.3m (H1 2025: $17.9m) with royalty and metal stream related revenue increasing 102% to $32.0m (H1 2025: $15.8m)"]}]}]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["159% increase in base metals portfolio contribution to $22.5m (H1 2025: $8.7m)"]}]}]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["509% increase in adjusted earnings to $19.5m (H1 2025: $3.2m)"]}]}]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Adjusted earnings per share of 7.81c (H1 2025: 1.27c)"]}]}]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Profit before tax of $24.3m (H1 2025: loss $10.9m)"]}]}]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Free cash flow of $12.1m (H1 2025: $2.0m)"]}]}]},{"type":"list","chi